// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR [E_FIBER_INDIRECT_CALL] indirect call inside a `spawn` body
//
// !!! RUN WITH `NOVA_FIBER_INDIRECT=1` SET !!! Приёмка интегратора
// 2026-08-06 (второй раунд, p238-f2): `E_FIBER_INDIRECT_CALL` is gated
// behind `NOVA_FIBER_INDIRECT=1` (default OFF) — the `Tag::Undecided`
// family (D446 §4's "непрямые вызовы недоказуемы без типизированной
// пометки на параметре") is a model LIMIT, not a proven finding, per the
// governing principle in `docs/plans/wip/PROGRESS-p238-f2.md` §4. WITHOUT
// the env var this file compiles CLEAN (`ok:`) — that is the CORRECT,
// intended default behavior, not a regression. If the authoritative
// conformance runner does not (yet) support per-fixture env vars, this
// file will show as an unexpected PASS under a vanilla run — flag for the
// integrator to either wire the env var into the runner for this fixture
// or move it out of the default-run set until the parameter-safety-marker
// mechanism (owner decision, not yet made) lets it become a permanent,
// always-on finding.

// Plan 238 Ф.2 (D446 §4/Ф.8-НОВАЯ П.2): a call reached inside a `spawn`
// body through a PARAMETER of function type — the concrete target is not
// statically knowable (any closure the caller passes could be substituted)
// — is conservatively treated as unsafe under the flag. This is the
// D446 §4 "непрямые вызовы" case, distinct from `E_FIBER_UNSAFE_CALL`
// (a resolved target whose бирка is `Tag::Unsafe`): here there is no
// target to even look up a бирка for.

module neg.fiber_indirect_call_neg

fn run_in_fiber(task fn() -> ()) {
    supervised {
        spawn {
            task()
        }
    }
}
